<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			31/7/97		  24/7/97		2/8/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    400			400	     375-400</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75			100		 50-75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,850	    1,800-1,825	 1,500-1,525</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	250-275			275		   425</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  10-15			 15		    25</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks were stable with barge movements in and out.</p>
<p>Naphtha inventories dipped as little product arrived.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks rose with cargoes coming from Russia and some departures down the Rhine.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories fell slightly as the ARA bunker sector absorbed material and vacuum gas oil moved into Germany. Some straight-run product arrived by cargo.</p>
<p>Jet fuel levels dipped as product moved to the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
